Workaround:
GLFWcursor\* CursorManager::BlankCursor()
{
    int w=1;//16;
    int h=1;//16;
    unsigned char pixels[w \* h \* 4];
    memset(pixels, 0x00, sizeof(pixels));
    GLFWimage image;
    image.width = w;
    image.height = h;
    image.pixels = pixels;
    return glfwCreateCursor(&image, 0, 0);
}

issue.body:
After upgrading to glfw 3.1 my programs (see minimal example below) just hang on glfwCreateWindow. Git bisect shows [this commit](https://github.com/glfw/glfw/commit/0c58df06d507) as the first bad commit. My guess this happens because [fluxbox](http://fluxbox.org/) does not support _NET_REQUEST_FRAME_EXTENTS ( http://fluxbox.sourceforge.net/docs/ewmh-support.html )

The same happens on git master.

program example:

``` c++
#include <GLFW/glfw3.h>
int main() {
    glfwInit();
    glfwCreateWindow(640, 480, "OpenGL", glfwGetPrimaryMonitor(), nullptr);
    glfwTerminate();
}
```
